Reel Edit 0.1 (test 1)
======================

Reel Edit is a video editor for RISC OS that is being written, on the MLT
multimedia framework (the engine of Shotcut and Kdenlive), with the
Raspberry Pi's video hardware through riscos-reelhwaccel. This test build
has its first window only: the Viewer, which plays a video or an MLT
project. The editing windows come next.

It needs RISC OS 5 on ARMv7 with VFP (Raspberry Pi 2, 3, 4), with
SharedUnixLibrary and ARMEABISupport (!Run checks). H.264 is decoded on
the Pi's VideoCore (1080p needs gpu_mem=128 in config.txt) and HEVC on the
Pi 4's HEVC block, the ARM taking over for anything they refuse. Sound
plays through SharedSoundBuffer.

Using it
--------
Double-click !ReelEdit: its icon goes on the icon bar. Drop a video, or an
MLT project (.mlt, from Shotcut, Kdenlive or melt), on the icon or on the
Viewer. Click the icon to bring the Viewer back to the front.

The Viewer: the picture above the controls: to the start, a frame back,
Play/Stop, a frame on, to the end, the position bar (click to go there)
and the timecode (hours:minutes:seconds:frames). Adjust on the frame
buttons moves a second.

Keys (click the Viewer first):
  Space        play / stop
  J  K  L      play backwards, stop, play forwards; J or L again: faster (x2, x4)
  Left Right   a frame back, forwards (Shift: a second)
  Home  Copy   the start, the end
  Escape       stop

While playing, the picture goes through the hardware overlay (VideoOverlay)
when it can; a menu or window over the picture, or stopping, draws it in
the window instead, so it can be seen under them. *Set ReelEdit$NoOverlay 1
never uses the overlay.

Log
---
Reel Edit writes what it did to <Wimp$ScrapDir>.ReelEditLog (each time it
starts): the file opened, the overlay, and once a second while playing the
pictures made and left out and the time it left to other programs. Please
send it with any report. *Set ReelEdit$Log to another file, or "off".

